Title OSRDNDisplay
Version 1.2
Description OPENSTEP 4.2 (i386) DriverKit display driver for the ATI Radeon 9250 (RV280, PCI 1002:5960; tested on revision 1 with 128 MiB). Five resolutions from 640x480 to 1600x1200 and four pixel formats; the greyscale format additionally takes a Gray Levels setting of 256, 16, 4 or 2, which changes only the palette. Installs the bundle into /private/Drivers/i386 and does NOT activate it: run Configure.app, add OSRDNDisplay to Active Drivers in System.config, and reboot. Recovery: type config=Default at the boot: prompt to come back with the original display driver. The bundle also carries the command processor and the 3D path the OSRDNMesaAccel package uses; 3D needs a board with at least 128 MiB, and on a smaller one the driver declines the 3D window and the display still works. Contains AMD's R200 CP microcode under its MIT notice, reproduced in /usr/local/Documentation/OpenStep-Radeon9250/NOTICE.
DefaultLocation /
DiskName OPENSTEP Radeon 9250 Display Intel
Application NO
Relocatable NO
NeedsAuthorization YES
DisableSparseInstall YES
DeleteWarning Removing this package removes only the driver bundle. If it is still listed in Active Drivers the machine will boot without a display driver, so remove it from System.config with Configure.app first.
